From: Pobega <pobega@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GCC 8.3 RTL LTO internal compiler error in sh4_interrupts

Work around GCC 8.3.0 internal compiler error (gen_reg_rtx at emit-rtl.c:1187)
during link-time optimization (LTO) on aarch64 toolchains (e.g. tg5040).
GCC 8.3 fails to compute the addresses of INTC_IPRA.reg_data, INTC_IPRB.reg_data,
and INTC_IPRC.reg_data in the static const InterruptSourceList initializer.
Indexing the underlying INTC MMIO array directly via ((const u16*)&INTC[1..3])
allows GCC 8.3 to emit the constant table without crashing.
---
 core/hw/sh4/sh4_interrupts.cpp | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/core/hw/sh4/sh4_interrupts.cpp b/core/hw/sh4/sh4_interrupts.cpp
index 49a3be455..56886e414 100644
--- a/core/hw/sh4/sh4_interrupts.cpp
+++ b/core/hw/sh4/sh4_interrupts.cpp
@@ -25,9 +25,9 @@ const u16 IRLPriority = 0x0246;
 #define IRLP11 &IRLPriority,4
 #define IRLP13 &IRLPriority,8
 
-#define GIPA(p) &INTC_IPRA.reg_data,4*p
-#define GIPB(p) &INTC_IPRB.reg_data,4*p
-#define GIPC(p) &INTC_IPRC.reg_data,4*p
+#define GIPA(p) ((const u16*)&INTC[1]),4*p
+#define GIPB(p) ((const u16*)&INTC[2]),4*p
+#define GIPC(p) ((const u16*)&INTC[3]),4*p
 
 struct InterptSourceList_Entry
 {
-- 
